    logP = 2.2);
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Clindamycin is a lincosamide antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections such as staphylococcal and skin infections, acne, dental abscesses, bacterial vaginosis, toxoplasmosis, and pneumocystosis. It is widely used in human medicine and is also approved for veterinary use, and it appears on the WHO list of essential medicines.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422273\">Wikidata Q422273</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>clindamycin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D10AF01, G01AA10, J01FF01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01190\">DB01190</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/446598\">446598</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:3745\">3745</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422273\">Q422273</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C18H33ClN2O5S</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>424.981 g/mol (PubChem CID 446598)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>2.2 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
end Clindamycin;
